  "summary": "Results inbox done: all 8 items closed under RBC-INBOX-01. Each patient was confirmed by two identifiers.\n\n- **pt-0010 Holloway, K 6.2 (not hemolyzed, creatinine 1.58, started lisinopril 10/06):** Messaged the on-call pool at stat priority (comm-t0002) and asked them to decide on holding lisinopril. Ordered a stat BMP (sr-t0001), messaged the patient (comm-t0003) and wrote a note (doc-t0004). RBC-LAB-03 §1.\n- **pt-0008 Brennan, K 6.4 (hemolyzed specimen):** Ordered an urgent repeat BMP to be drawn by Mon 10/26 (sr-t0006) and messaged the patient to come in (comm-t0007). On-call was not notified, per policy. Note written (doc-t0008). RBC-LAB-03 §2.\n- **pt-0053 Ruiz, age 16, knee X-ray showing an aggressive lytic lesion of the lower femur that may be a bone tumour:** Ordered an urgent MRI of the femur with and without contrast (sr-t0010) and an urgent orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0011), both due by 11/05. Each has a scheduling tracking task (task-t0012, task-t0013). Messaged the patient and guardian (comm-t0015). Assigned RN triage a call to his mother today (task-t0014). Note written (doc-t0016). RBC-RAD-05 §3–4.\n- **pt-0013 Marsh, outside CT from June with a 5 mm right lower lobe lung nodule:** This is the same nodule already being followed in lung cancer screening (Lung-RADS 2 on 9/15/2025). Her yearly screening CT window has passed, so I ordered a low-dose screening CT chest for 10/23–11/06 (sr-t0018). Added a tracking task (task-t0019), messaged the patient (comm-t0020) and wrote a note (doc-t0021). RBC-RAD-05 §2.\n- **pt-0006 Patel, positive stool test (FIT):** Dr. Lin already placed an active GI referral for colonoscopy (sr-t2-gi-1020). I linked it and did not place a second one, per RBC-GI-01 §2. Messaged the patient (comm-t0023) and wrote a note (doc-t0024).\n- **pt-0007 kidney ultrasound:** Simple renal cyst; the radiologist says no follow-up imaging is needed. Closed with a comment that no follow-up is needed under RBC-INBOX-01 §3.\n- **pt-0016 TSH and lipid panel:** Both normal; acknowledged and closed.\n\n**Still open, assigned to others:**\n- The on-call pool's review of Ms. Holloway.\n- The RN triage call to Tomás Ruiz's mother.\n- The scheduling tracking tasks, due 11/05 and 11/06.",
